[Music]  hey guys it's Jonah here so you're doing  your exercises you're paying attention  to your food intake but the weight just  won't budge you're wondering what on  earth am I doing wrong  well what should this video through as I  will be sharing with you ten common  reasons why you're not losing weight  number one your expectations are  unrealistic I've been receiving too many  comments asking me how can I lose 10  kilos in a month or even a week my  simple answer is look it did not take  you one month to put on 10 kilos it  probably took you over several months or  even years for the weight to slowly  creep on hence it will take your time to  lose weight the safe and sustainable  weight loss is between 1 to 2 pounds a  week so don't set yourself unrealistic  expectations because then you're only  setting yourself up for failure you get  frustrated when you don't see results as  quickly as you hope to if you have lost  some weight and you feel good about  yourself but the skill doesn't seem to  want to budge any further then perhaps  it is time for you to learn to accept  and love your body the way it is because  at some point your weight will reach a  healthy set mark and it won't budge any  further to try to go beyond that will be  unhealthy so set yourself realistic and  achievable goals the second reason is  you are losing without realizing it it  is very important for us to understand  that our weight fluctuates every single  day it can fluctuate up to 5 pounds in a  day so if you were to measure yourself  in the morning afternoon and in the  evening chances are you will have 3  different measurements so this is due to  the amount of water in the body so  throughout the day our body will hold on  to the fluids from food and also drinks  hence that is why you tend to feel  lighter in the morning and heavier  towards the evening your weight loss  progress should not just be measured by  the number on the scale this is in fact  the least most accurate way to measure  your weight loss progress because we  want to be losing body fat not just  weight we can be gaining muscles and  losing weight at the same time this is  especially common if you just started  exercising so instead of stepping on the  scale and allowing a VAT  number two determine how well you're  doing take your body measurements and  see how well your clothes are fitting  you if your clothes are fitting you  better but the skill just one badge well  that just means that you are losing body  fat by you're putting on muscles which  is a great thing and you should not be  worried about it next you're bingeing  unhealthy food I'm sure you have seen  this phrase guilt-free treats every so  often nowadays a lot of us tend to have  the mindset that just because a food is  categorized as healthy that gives us the  permission to eat as much as we want  because hey it's good for you and it  will do you no harm but what you might  feel to realize is that one slice of  healthy raw cake might have the same  amount of calories as a slice of  chocolate cake so just because something  is healthy that doesn't mean that you  can help yourself to several servings  and fool yourself into thinking that it  will not affect your weight loss  progress it is important to know that  even if something is really healthy the  calories still count so treat yourself  in moderation you've been doing the same  thing over and over again so if you have  been on the same routine and losing  weight for many months and you have hit  a plateau then perhaps you just need to  take a break okay brick for your workout  a break from your diet and just try  something completely different sleep  more eat more than you're used to try  new activities and just take it easy the  more stressed out you are about losing  weight and the harder it is for you to  progress so instead of just focusing on  the end goal it is very important for  you to enjoy the entire journey the next  reason is you're not drinking enough  water ask yourself are you drinking  between 2.5 to 3 liters of water every  single day drinking enough water is so  easy to forget but it is crucial to your  weight loss success if your body is  dehydrated if your workout and your  progress will suffer oftentimes we think  we're hungry but we're really just  thirsty so the next time you feel hungry  instead of grabbing snacks and start  munching drink water first and ask  yourself if you're truly hungry or just  dehydrated drinking water before a meal  can also make you feel fuller as  result you will eat less the next point  you're drinking your calories are you  one of those people who enjoy fruit  juices soda drinks fancy coffee or even  alcohol liquid calories in just about  any form of sneaky calories those drinks  are loaded with calories and some may  even contain more calories than a proper  meal just by eliminating liquid calories  you can save up to 500 calories in a day  and you will see a huge difference to  your weight loss progress next you're  probably not lifting weights are you a  cardio bunny  if so chances are you look skinny fat  with no muscle tone it is time to lift  some weights okay weight lifting can  help to build and preserve a muscle mass  and prevent metabolic slowdown when you  only do cardio you've been fat only  during the workout and it stops shortly  after the workout now if you include  strength training your body continues to  burn fat even after the workout while at  rest and this is also known as the after  burn effect which can speed up weight  loss stress are you overwhelmed are you  constantly on the go do you struggle to  even breathe properly or do you have  issues that you have to deal with  whatever reason stress can be the  underlying cause of your witness  struggle especially weight around the  belly that's because of the hormone  called cortisol which makes your body  hold on to fat so if you're someone who  is very disciplined in your workout and  food intake but you struggle to lose  belly fat ask yourself what is your  stress level like if it means taking 10  minutes in the evening to wind down I  would recommend you to do that because  it can make a huge difference to your  weight loss progress what I like to do  is light up scented candles and reflect  on the positive things in my day it  helps me to sleep better and I wake up  feeling more energized thus another  stress relates a problem is lack of  sleep when you do not get enough rest  your hormones go crazy boosting the  levels of ghrelin which increases your  appetite you're basically putting your  body into carb and fat survival mode  your metabolism slows down because it's  trying to maintain its resources but at  the same time your body wants more food  that is when the late night snacking  starts to take over just to keep you  awake and finally you're too focused on  dieting if there is one thing you can do  right now is ditch the word dieting when  we think of dieting it is often  associated to restriction short-term and  unsustainable regimes most people who  have the mindset of dieting tend to gain  more weight over time so ditch dieting  and change that to healthy eating focus  on nourishing your body with good food  instead of depriving it and weight loss  will happen as a natural side effect  because primarily our goal is to be  fitter healthier and live a more  fulfilled life so I hope that this video  will help you to take another look at  your fitness journey ok instead of just  being obsessed over the number on the  skill or being so obsessed over our  goals it is very important to enjoy the  entire journey so be sure to give this  video a thumb up share with your friends  and subscribe to my youtube channel for  a lot more fitness tips nutritional tips  recipes workout videos and don't forget  to turn on your notification button so  that you will get notified every time I  upload a new video all the best

